<title>FRANCE: Paris Metro workers' union sets Friday strike.</title>
<headline>Paris Metro workers' union sets Friday strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The communist-led CGT trade union has given notice of strike action on the Paris metro, regional express train and bus network from Thursday night to Saturday morning, the union said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The largest union of Paris public transport and maintenance workers urged members to strike for two hours at the end of each shift to demand more jobs, a pay rise and better working conditions while the RATP transport authority board meets on Friday.</p>
<p>An RATP spokesman said it was not clear how the staggered stoppages would affect passenger services.</p>
</text>
